    {
      "v": 4,
      "zh": "不要惧怕，因你必不致蒙羞；也不要抱愧，因你必不致受辱。你必忘记幼年的羞愧，不再记念你寡居的羞辱。",
      "en": "Don’t be afraid, for you will not be put to shame.Don’t be intimidated,[NOTE:1] for you will not be humiliated.You will forget about the shame you experienced in your youth;you will no longer remember the disgrace of your abandonment.[NOTE:2]",
      "notes": [
        "Or “embarrassed”; NASB “humiliated…disgraced.”",
        "Another option is to translate, “the disgrace of our widowhood” (so NRSV). However, the following context (vv. 6-7) refers to Zion’s husband, the Lord, abandoning her, not dying. This suggests that an אַלְמָנָה (ʾalmanah) was a woman who had lost her husband, whether by death or abandonment."
